  "Content policy summary": "Kûrû-tënë ti Ndïä ti Kontenü",
  "Continue to site": "Gue Na Site",
  "Convert rights declarations into a workable licensing market instead of a binary open/closed web.": "Gbïan wärängö ti dröa aga marché ti licence so ayeke sâra kua nzönî, aga internet so ayeke gï «azi/akanga» oko pëpe.",
  "Copied ✓": "A Kopî Awe ✓",
  "Copy": "Kopî",
  "Correct positioning: independent research drafts, protocol proposals, and an open specification experiment.": "Ndo so alîngbi: ambeti-kôzo ti gïngö-ndo so ayeke indépendant, atënë ti protocole, na tapande ti spécification so azi.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Belgium (BE) now maps to Dutch instead of French — Flemish speakers are the country’s majority (~60%) over Walloon French speakers (~40%).": "A lëke lêgë ti kôzo: Belgique (BE) fadësô ague na yângâ Néerlandais aga na Français — azo so atene Flamand ayeke gbâ kötä ti kodoro (~60%) ahon azo so atene Français ti Wallon (~40%).",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Kazakhstan (KZ) now maps to Kazakh instead of Russian, now that a Kazakh translation exists — the same kind of fix as the earlier Belgium correction.": "A lëke lêgë ti kôzo: Kazakhstan (KZ) fadësô ague na yângâ Kazakh aga na Russe, ndâli ti so fadësô traduction ti Kazakh ayeke — oko lëkëngö tongana ti Belgique kôzo.",
  "Could AI Be Conscious?": "Could AI Be Conscious?",
  "Crawler access rules": "Andïä ti Lêgë ti Crawler",
  "Crawler simulator": "Simulateur ti Crawler",
  "Currency": "Nginza",
  "Custom tier": "Nivo ti Mo Mvenî",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous afa tënë ti mbeti so a zîa ni na Journal of Medical Ethics so a kanga ni, na yâ ni angbâti mingi so IA agiris ni, na aïri ti université so ayeke tâ pëpe na adresse email so a sâra kua na ni pëpe — so wa-sû, atene, azîa ni tongana ni, atâ na peko ti so a mû lêgë na lo tî lëke épreuve. Mbeti so akângbi ni na Bioethics, so bâa-nzönî ti ni ti citation so ayeke sâra kua terê ni, alîngbi tî bâa kpälë so — na atene so kpälë ni ayeke technologie ti bâa pëpe (script ti zo oko afa acitation so ayeke bübä na yâ ti ngbonga kete ahon minute oko), me ayeke kua ti awa-bâa-nzönî so azo afuta ala pëpe, na andïä ti sigigi so amû lêgë na gbâ ahon bâa nzönî.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Sarango Donnée na Futa Pëpe, na Ngele ti IA so ayeke na Trillion Dollar",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis afa tënë ti bûngbi ti gbötöngö so ayeke tongana FINRA, ndali ti sigigi ti amodèle ti IA so kötä ahon: alaboratoire afüngä amodèle ti ala ti bâa juska lâ 30 kôzo na peko ti sigigi, na kôzo a yeke gï na yëngö, na lêgë ti gue juska na ndïä so ayeke hunda na terê, na marché ti USA.",
  "Denied": "A Kanga Ni",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Modèle ti Londo ti Ndïä so Alîngbi tî Zîa",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Modèle ti londo ti ndïä na /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — site kete so ayeke na undêrê kûê so masïni alîngbi tî diko, so alëke awe ndali ti Cloudflare Pages wala host oko oko.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Zïängö Andïä so Masïni Alîngbi tî Diko na Site ti Mo",
  "Disclaimer": "Avertissement",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Aga nde na UI ti zo, SEO, wala API so ayeke gï tongaso, «AI Ingestion & Capability Layer» amû na asite lëkëngö so andö na masïni: undêrê ti Manifest (lêgë ti lïngö tongana /llms.txt na /ai/manifest.json), undêrê ti Corpus (hïngängö-ye so masïni alîngbi tî diko), undêrê ti Capability (angbêne so agent alîngbi tî appeler), na undêrê ti Gouvernance (londo, licence, version). Ayeke kôzo na static, alîngbi tî kono juska na API na MCP. Fängö-iri: na mbeti so, AICL ayeke iri ti lëkëngö ti mängängö-kontenü; na apage ti protocole ti site so, AICL ayeke fa Undêrê ti Licence ti Kontenü ti IA.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Ambeti",
  "Docs / Examples": "Ambeti / Atapande",
  "Document library": "Ndo-Bûngbi ti Mbeti",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "IA ayeke na dröa mä — na alêgë ti bâa ni wa ayeke na nda-tënë tâ tâ?",
  "Download": "Gbû na Ndo ti Mo",
  "Draft status": "Statut ti Mbeti-Kôzo",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Tapande ti mändängö: HMAC-SHA256 na yâ ti sïrî so azo mîngi ahinga ni, so afa atoken ti licence so andïä na hunda, na ngbonga, na alîngbi tî bâa nzönî. Atoken ti tâ sarango a lîngbi tî sû iri na ni na lêgë ûse, na clé ti gîgî ti wa-sigigi so azo alîngbi tî wara na gbe ti /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Ambeti mïnäna na yâ ti /topics, fadësô so agent ti IA agi ala, aga na maboko ti zo pëpe — oko ndïä tongana kôzo: yângâ-ndâ oko oko a wara ni na a bâa nzönî fadësô, akûrû-tënë ayeke tënë ti e mvenî, kôzo ti zîa ye. Ambeti 14 kûê.",
  "Email": "Email",
  "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model": "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model",
  "Empirical Research": "Gïngö-Ndo so Ayeke na Tapande",
  "English edition →": "Édition Anglais →",
  "Ensure openness is machine-executable — so goodwill is not discarded as legal uncertainty.": "Bâa so zïngö ayeke ye so masïni alîngbi tî sâra kua na ndö ni — ti si nzönî-bê agirisa aga bê-ûse ti ndïä pëpe.",
  "Epistemology": "Épistémologie",
